  "confirmBitlockerHead": "Your Windows drive is encrypted with BitLocker",
  "confirmBitlockerScript": "Installing replaces the boot loader that runs first at start-up. The Windows tool has already suspended BitLocker, so the next 2 restarts should not ask for the recovery key. If one does, find it at aka.ms/myrecoverykey using the key ID shown on screen.",
  "confirmBitlockerUsb": "Installing replaces the boot loader that runs first at start-up. The next time you start Windows it will probably ask for the 48-digit recovery key: the screen shows a key ID; look it up at aka.ms/myrecoverykey. Without the key you cannot get into Windows, so make sure you can get it before you continue.",
