  "riskTitle": "Read this first: what follows can destroy your data",
  "riskSub": "The next steps change this disk. Read all of it — the button below unlocks only after you have read to the end, waited, and ticked the box.",
  "riskExpHead": "This is an experimental community port",
  "riskExpBody": "This Android is a hobbyist port, not a product of Huawei, Qualcomm or Google. No vendor supports it, and nobody is responsible for your data. The installer has been tested on real hardware in only a few situations (see “What has been tested on real hardware” in the install guide).",
  "riskDiskHead": "Changes to the disk may be irreversible",
  "riskDiskBody": "What follows changes this disk’s partition table and what is inside its partitions. A bug, a disk fault or a power cut can corrupt your data or lose all of it. These changes are irreversible: the installer cannot undo them and cannot promise to get your data back afterwards.",
  "riskWipeHead": "Erase the whole disk: everything on it is deleted",
  "riskWipeBody": "Every partition on this disk is deleted — Windows, your files, any other system and the recovery partitions, all of it. To use Windows again afterwards you would have to install it from scratch from a Windows USB stick.",
  "riskAlongHead": "Keep the current system: the disk still changes",
  "riskAlongBody": "Android goes only into free space and existing partitions are neither shrunk nor deleted, but the partition table is rewritten and a boot loader is put into the EFI partition both systems share. If any step goes wrong, the existing system may fail to start too.",
  "riskReinstallHead": "Reinstall Android",
  "riskReinstallWipe": "Android’s system partitions are rewritten and /data is erased: installed apps, photos, chats and everything else stored in Android are lost.",
  "riskReinstallKeep": "Android’s system partitions are rewritten; you chose to keep /data. But after moving to an older version, or if the install fails halfway, the kept data may become unreadable — back it up all the same.",
  "riskWinHead": "Windows and the BitLocker recovery key",
  "riskWinBody": "Installing puts a boot loader into the EFI partition both systems share and replaces the file that runs first at start-up (the original is backed up). If Windows uses BitLocker or “device encryption”, it may ask for the recovery key next time — without the key you can never get into Windows again, and its data cannot be read. Before you continue, make sure you can get the key at aka.ms/myrecoverykey.",
  "riskWinBitlocker": "This disk does have a BitLocker-encrypted volume: the final confirmation page will ask you to confirm that you have the recovery key.",
  "riskShrinkHead": "Shrinking an existing partition",
  "riskShrinkBody": "Shrinking a partition moves data around inside its file system. If Windows was not fully shut down (hibernation, Fast Startup) or the partition already has errors, shrinking can damage it so that Windows no longer starts. A BitLocker-protected Windows may also ask for its recovery key at the next start (aka.ms/myrecoverykey).",
  "riskEditHead": "Adjusting the disk by hand",
  "riskEditBody": "Deleting or formatting wipes a partition’s data at once; shrinking and growing move data inside its file system. Use this only if you know what every partition is — deleting the wrong one can leave Windows or Android unable to start.",
  "riskBackupHead": "Back up now",
  "riskBackupBody": "Copy your important files (photos, documents, anything in Windows, app data in Android) to another device, an external drive or cloud storage. A copy on another partition of this same disk does not count — it is at the same risk. If you have not backed up yet, tap Back now, shut down, back up, and come back afterwards.",
  "riskPowerHead": "Keep the power connected",
  "riskPowerBody": "Plug in the power adapter before you start and leave it in until the end. If power is lost or the battery runs out halfway, the disk is left half-written: nothing may start and data may be damaged. Do not hold the power button or force a restart while it runs.",
  "riskNoCancelHead": "Once writing starts, it cannot be cancelled",
  "riskNoCancelInstall": "The next page is the final confirmation. Once you hold the button there, writing starts; it cannot be cancelled or undone (when installing over the network, the download can still be cancelled — the disk is not touched until it has finished).",
  "riskNoCancelStep": "Each operation on the next page runs as soon as you hold its button: it cannot be stopped midway and there is no undo afterwards.",
